   "note": "Load holding fails during a slow leak at 18 degrees, so the walker is lost either way; the models differ in which comes first. Level 1 ties leg force and centre-of-pressure authority to the same capacity (A3, A4) and tips. Level 2 tipped with the earlier assumed torques (ankle 20, knee 60 kN m); with the adopted ankle 26.5 kN m or knee 22.5 kN m (DQ-012), either change alone, the ankle outlasts the knees, the legs fold and the cockpit drops at about 2.8 m/s (the HAZ-PIL-002 mechanism, against 4.1 m/s after a burst)."
  },
