   "note": "A slow leak at 16.5 degrees with load holding working; the pilot's protective stop starts at 3.9 s with 49% capacity. Level 1 plants the second foot, crouches and loses balance as its centre-of-pressure limit shrinks (A3), tipping 45 ms after the hold engages. Level 2 does not complete the stop step at that capacity, stays on the stance foot and holds it with the ankle until the hold engages; with the adopted torques it tips only with the ankle at or below about 12 kN m. The case sits on the actuator-capacity boundary (sim/results/sizing-cf4.md)."
  }
